Found by k256. lib/OCP/Cmd/Apply/K8s.pm resource_exists and crd_get turn every failed read into "not there". resource_exists backs OCP::Cmd::Apply::AMDGPU::ds_present, so a 403 there makes apply redeploy (or remove) an AMD component it could not see, and AMDGPU::not_ready reports any failed read as "not found".

Done when only a 404 is absent, any other failure dies or is reported with its cause (callers decide; check every caller of both), AMDGPU says "could not read" instead of "not found", and tests pin 404 vs 403 vs 500. Lane: ocp-apply-worker.

2026-10-31 02:46 Change in: K8s.pm resource_exists dies 'could not read KIND ns/name: <cause>' unless the exception matches /\b404\b/; crd_get returns undef only on status 404, dies on transport error, any other >=400 (HTTP status + body excerpt) and on a 200 that is no JSON. Callers: AMDGPU setup's remove decision catches ds_present per component (unreadable -> that component's error result, nothing removed, others carry on); ensure needs no change (ds_present dies inside setup's per-component eval -> no deploy, no restored/updated); not_ready gets read_or_why: 404 '<what> not found', else 'could not read <what>: <cause>' for the DaemonSet, the Node and the ResourceSlices reads (poll reads again, wait_ready dies with the last why). Workloads post-deploy ClusterPolicy state poll and Network Gateway Accepted poll eval their read, poll again, and name the last failed read (WARN on STDERR / in the death). Registry running, NFD, GPU operator running/toolkit/CRD/ClusterPolicy diff reads: no code change, they now die and their step reports [!!].

